 'faq_heading'=>'Mold removal questions from West Vancouver property owners','faqs'=>[['Can mold be removed without taking down drywall?','It depends on the material and extent. Surface growth from condensation may sometimes be cleaned, but drywall with established growth, water damage or concealed impact may require removal.'],['Will mold return after removal?','Mold can return if moisture returns. Correcting leaks, condensation, humidity and ventilation issues is essential to reducing the chance of recurrence.'],['Can I stay in the property during the work?','That depends on the size and location of the project, the occupants and the containment plan. Access and occupancy should be discussed before work begins.'],['How long does mold removal take?','A small focused project may take less time than work involving several rooms, concealed cavities, drying or coordination with plumbing and building repairs. The scope determines the schedule.'],['Do you remove black mold?','Dark coloured mold can be removed using methods based on the affected material and extent. Colour alone does not identify the mold or determine the removal plan.'],['Is testing required after mold removal?','Not for every project. Visual review, moisture conditions and cleaning records may be sufficient for some work. Independent post remediation verification can be useful when it is part of the agreed scope.']]
